  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Spoiler Text\n\nA phrase in a sentence hides under a shimmering field of specks, then a wave blows them away and the words come into focus.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A sentence has one phrase that should be teased, then revealed: a twist, a price, a punchline.\n- A chat-style or social video needs the 'tap to reveal spoiler' moment.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The whole text should appear with a plain reveal: use blur-in or mask-reveal-up.\n- The hidden part is long: the patch dominates the frame.\n\nVariables:\n- before (string): Text before, default \"Same. When it turned out\"\n- spoiler (string): Hidden phrase, default \"the lighthouse keeper had been writing the letters all along\"\n- after (string): Text after, default \"I had to pause it for a minute.\"\n- font_size (number, 16-160): Font size, default 56\n- color (color): Text color, default \"#3f3f46\"\n- speck_color (color): Speck color, default \"#18181b\"\n- reveal_at (number, 0.2-10): Reveal at, default 2.4\n- reveal_from (enum): Reveal from, default \"left\"\n- seed (number, 1-9999): Seed, default 7\n\nSource: https://github.com/kokonut-labs/kokonutui. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Spoiler Text\n\n  A phrase inside a sentence is hidden under a shimmering field of drifting specks, like a chat-app spoiler; at the reveal a wave blows the specks away while the words come into focus.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/kokonut-labs/kokonutui/blob/4d497b7b03f02ffd07225e638c0b9ace3f892dbb/components/kokonutui/spoiler-text.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2025 kokonutUI\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"spoiler-text\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"5\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"before\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Text before\", \"description\": \"Visible text before the hidden phrase.\", \"default\": \"Same. When it turned out\"},\n    {\"id\": \"spoiler\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Hidden phrase\", \"description\": \"The phrase hidden under the specks until the reveal.\", \"default\": \"the lighthouse keeper had been writing the letters all along\"},\n    {\"id\": \"after\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Text after\", \"description\": \"Visible text after the hidden phrase.\", \"default\": \"I had to pause it for a minute.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Text size in pixels.\", \"default\": 56, \"min\": 16, \"max\": 160, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Text color\", \"description\": \"Color of the text.\", \"default\": \"#3f3f46\"},\n    {\"id\": \"speck_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Speck color\", \"description\": \"Color of the specks and the soft patch behind them.\", \"default\": \"#18181b\"},\n    {\"id\": \"reveal_at\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Reveal at\", \"description\": \"Second the specks are blown away.\", \"default\": 2.4, \"min\": 0.2, \"max\": 10, \"step\": 0.1, \"unit\": \"s\"},\n    {\"id\": \"reveal_from\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Reveal from\", \"description\": \"Where the wave starts.\", \"default\": \"left\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"left\", \"label\": \"Start of the phrase\"}, {\"value\": \"center\", \"label\": \"Middle of the phrase\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"seed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Seed\", \"description\": \"Same seed scatters the same specks every time.\", \"default\": 7, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 9999, \"step\": 1}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Spoiler Text</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600&amp;display=block\" />\n      <style>\n        #root { position: absolute; inset: 0; overflow: hidden; container-type: size; pointer-events: none; }\n        #root { color: var(--sp-color, #3f3f46); font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, system-ui, sans-serif); }\n        .sp-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .sp-text { width: 82%; line-height: 1.5; font-weight: 500; text-wrap: pretty; }\n        .sp-spoiler { position: relative; border-radius: 0.12em; -webkit-box-decoration-break: clone; box-decoration-break: clone; background: var(--sp-patch, rgba(24,24,27,0.06)); }\n        .sp-phrase { display: inline; opacity: 0; filter: blur(6px); }\n        .sp-canvas { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"spoiler-text\" data-duration=\"5\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"sp-clip\" class=\"sp-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"5\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <p id=\"sp-text\" class=\"sp-text\"><span id=\"sp-before\"></span> <span id=\"sp-spoiler\" class=\"sp-spoiler\"><span id=\"sp-phrase\" class=\"sp-phrase\"></span></span> <span id=\"sp-after\"></span></p>\n        </div>\n        <canvas id=\"sp-canvas\" class=\"sp-canvas\"></canvas>\n\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/CustomEase.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars = window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables() : {};\n            function num(v, f, a, b) { var x = Number(v); return Number.isFinite(x) ? Math.min(b, Math.max(a, x)) : f; }\n            function str(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && v.trim() ? v : f; }\n            function col(v, f) { return typeof v === \"string\" && v ? v : f; }\n            function mulberry32(a) { return function () { a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a); t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t; return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; }; }\n            function clamp01(x) { return x < 0 ? 0 : x > 1 ? 1 : x; }\n\n\n            var textEl = document.getElementById(\"sp-text\");\n            var spoiler = document.getElementById(\"sp-spoiler\");\n            var phrase = document.getElementById(\"sp-phrase\");\n            var canvas = document.getElementById(\"sp-canvas\");\n            document.getElementById(\"sp-before\").textContent = str(vars.before, \"Same. When it turned out\");\n            phrase.textContent = str(vars.spoiler, \"the lighthouse keeper had been writing the letters all along\");\n            document.getElementById(\"sp-after\").textContent = str(vars.after, \"I had to pause it for a minute.\");\n            var size = num(vars.font_size, 56, 16, 160);\n            var revealAt = num(vars.reveal_at, 2.4, 0.2, 10);\n            var fromCenter = String(vars.reveal_from) === \"center\";\n            var seed = num(vars.seed, 7, 1, 9999);\n            var speckColor = col(vars.speck_color, \"#18181b\");\n            root.style.setProperty(\"--sp-color\", col(vars.color, \"#3f3f46\"));\n            textEl.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n\n            var W = root.clientWidth, H = root.clientHeight;\n            canvas.width = W; canvas.height = H;\n            var ctx = canvas.getContext(\"2d\");\n\n            // Measure each line of the hidden phrase, in root pixels.\n            var rootBox = root.getBoundingClientRect();\n            var k = W / (rootBox.width || W);\n            var boxes = Array.prototype.map.call(spoiler.getClientRects(), function (r) {\n              return { l: (r.left - rootBox.left) * k, t: (r.top - rootBox.top) * k, r: (r.right - rootBox.left) * k, b: (r.bottom - rootBox.top) * k };\n            });\n            var first = boxes[0];\n            var origin = fromCenter\n              ? { x: boxes.reduce(function (s, b) { return s + (b.l + b.r) / 2; }, 0) / boxes.length, y: boxes.reduce(function (s, b) { return s + (b.t + b.b) / 2; }, 0) / boxes.length }\n              : { x: first.l + 4, y: (first.t + first.b) / 2 };\n            var bounds = boxes.reduce(function (a, b) { return { l: Math.min(a.l, b.l), t: Math.min(a.t, b.t), r: Math.max(a.r, b.r), b: Math.max(a.b, b.b) }; }, { l: 1e9, t: 1e9, r: -1e9, b: -1e9 });\n            var maxDist = Math.max(\n              Math.hypot(origin.x - bounds.l, origin.y - bounds.t), Math.hypot(origin.x - bounds.r, origin.y - bounds.t),\n              Math.hypot(origin.x - bounds.l, origin.y - bounds.b), Math.hypot(origin.x - bounds.r, origin.y - bounds.b));\n\n            // Specks: seeded, so the same seed always scatters the same field.\n            var rnd = mulberry32(seed);\n            var dot = Math.max(1.5, size / 22);\n            var DRIFT = size * 0.5, THROW = size * 1.6, WAVE = 0.52, FADE = 0.36;\n            var specks = [];\n            var area = boxes.reduce(function (s, b) { return s + (b.r - b.l) * (b.b - b.t); }, 0);\n            var scale = Math.min(1, 7000 / Math.max(1, area / (dot * dot * 3)));\n            boxes.forEach(function (b, bi) {\n              var w = b.r - b.l, h = b.b - b.t;\n              var n = Math.round((w * h / (dot * dot * 3)) * scale);\n              for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                var ang = rnd() * Math.PI * 2, sp = DRIFT * (0.3 + rnd() * 0.7);\n                var s = { x: b.l + rnd() * w, y: b.t + rnd() * h, vx: Math.cos(ang) * sp, vy: Math.sin(ang) * sp, ph: rnd(), rate: 0.35 + rnd() * 0.9, size: rnd() < 0.18 ? dot * 1.5 : dot, box: b, push: THROW * (0.5 + rnd()) };\n                var d = Math.hypot(s.x - origin.x, s.y - origin.y);\n                // The wave radius is maxDist * easeOut(u), easeOut(u) = 1 - (1-u)^3, so a speck at distance d is hit at u = 1 - (1 - d/maxDist)^(1/3).\n                var q = Math.min(1, d / maxDist);\n                s.hit = revealAt + WAVE * (1 - Math.pow(1 - q, 1 / 3));\n                specks.push(s);\n              }\n            });\n            // A speck bounces around inside its own line until the wave reaches it.\n            function bounce(v, lo, hi) {\n              var span = hi - lo; if (span <= 0) return lo;\n              var m = (v - lo) % (2 * span); if (m < 0) m += 2 * span;\n              return lo + (m > span ? 2 * span - m : m);\n            }\n            function paint(t) {\n              ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);\n              ctx.fillStyle = speckColor;\n              for (var i = 0; i < specks.length; i++) {\n                var s = specks[i];\n                var tt = Math.min(t, s.hit);\n                var x = bounce(s.x + s.vx * tt, s.box.l, s.box.r), y = bounce(s.y + s.vy * tt, s.box.t, s.box.b);\n                var fade = 1;\n                if (t > s.hit) {\n                  var dt = t - s.hit;\n                  fade = 1 - dt / FADE;\n                  if (fade <= 0) continue;\n                  var dx = x - origin.x, dy = y - origin.y, len = Math.hypot(dx, dy) || 1;\n                  x += s.vx * dt + (dx / len) * s.push * dt;\n                  y += s.vy * dt + (dy / len) * s.push * dt;\n                }\n                var f = (s.ph + s.rate * tt) % 1;\n                var tw = 0.35 + 0.65 * Math.abs(Math.sin(f * Math.PI));\n                ctx.globalAlpha = tw * fade * 0.9;\n                ctx.fillRect(x, y, s.size, s.size);\n              }\n              ctx.globalAlpha = 1;\n            }\n\n            gsap.registerPlugin(CustomEase);\n            var easeOut = CustomEase.create(\"sp-out\", \"M0,0 C0.23,1 0.32,1 1,1\");\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            // The words come into focus and the soft patch clears at the reveal (0.45 s).\n            tl.to(phrase, { opacity: 1, filter: \"blur(0px)\", duration: 0.45, ease: easeOut }, revealAt);\n            tl.to(spoiler, { \"--sp-patch\": \"rgba(24,24,27,0)\", duration: 0.45, ease: easeOut }, revealAt);\n            var dur = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"5\");\n            var clock = { t: 0 };\n            tl.to(clock, { t: dur, duration: dur, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { paint(clock.t); } }, 0);\n            paint(0);\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"5\");\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"spoiler-text\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
 "sha256": "ceb32e68ea09889cf3a35c0d2534ac7adf67103220a467450e272f87f836e58e",
